3.2 Payments — critical
(Not production-ready)

The payment code generates a token, inserts a pending payment, and returns the token to the frontend.

However, the actual MTN MoMo and Airtel Money payment requests are not implemented. The code even contains a TODO for triggering the provider API.

The webhook code is also incomplete:

It trusts a simulated SUCCESSFUL status in the request body.
It does not verify the provider's webhook signature.
It does not verify the actual amount received.
It does not verify the currency.
It does not safely prevent simultaneous duplicate webhook processing.
It does not atomically create the purchase and update wallets.
It credits the artist wallet but does not credit the platform wallet's 30% share.
It does not properly implement the escrow process.
It does not implement Stripe payment processing.
This means the payment code is a starting example, not a functioning financial system.

My recommendation: Build the payment engine around verified provider transactions, database transactions, idempotency, and an immutable financial ledger. Never grant permanent access merely because someone submits a matching token.

