3.4 Video security and the 30-second preview
The specification says video URLs must not be exposed directly and that playback should use short-lived access tokens.

But the supplied code uses getPublicUrl() and returns video_url to the frontend.

That conflicts with the security requirement.

The 30-second player implementation also uses an alert when the preview ends. It does not provide a complete purchase overlay or secure playback restriction. A viewer may attempt to seek beyond the preview unless the server also controls playback access.

The correct design needs:

Private video storage.
Authenticated playback authorization.
Short-lived playback URLs or streaming tokens.
Server-side entitlement checks.
Preview restrictions that cannot be bypassed simply by seeking.
Permanent access after a verified purchase.
